Z||000010||Black88GT||09-07-2000||10:35 PM||||I had Cal Ripken, Jr. look at my yellow formula when I had it.  At the Oriole games they used to have a parking lot where all the players would park.  Of course it was fenced in and guarded and all.  I used to go to mainly check out their cars.  Rafael Palmeiro had the nicest Ferrari conv.  Anyway, I parked my formula real close to the fence and waited for the players to come out in hopes of getting an autographed ball, but I was kind of late and all of them were gone except Ripken.  He was always the last one out (he signed autographs at the end of the game for hours) and his Suburban was one of the only cars on the lot.  Some of the guards noticed me and came over to talk.  We were talking about the game when he came out.  The guards walked over to talk to him and one of them mentioned I was waiting for an autograph.  So he came over and signed my baseball, and my car was like right behind me<BR>and he said "is that your car?" and I was like "yeah, its a fiero" and he said "oh yeah I remember them" and then I said thanks and he left.  Well its not that great of a story but it made my day.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||6
